  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Song for Layne Staley**: rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Crying on Eddie Nash's Grave**: rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Untitled Song for the Singer from Viking**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [2]\n- **There Will Be No Divorce**: back after 42 archived shows (850 days) [2]\n- **Sept 19 Triple X Love! Love!**: back after 245 archived shows (3820 days); rare: 12 archived performances [2]\n- **Days**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 4 archived performances [2]\n- **Through this Fire**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2026-08-14** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 25 songs; 116 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children [1]\n- The audience stood for This Year, sat, then stood again for No Children and the encore [1]\n- John was elated with the engaged-yet-silent crowd at the gorgeous Taft Theatre [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2026-08-14**: taped by Kyle Kennelly & Emerald Green; transferred by Kyle Kennelly; source: SBD > PCM A10 (24/48 WAV) + FR-AV2 > DPA 4060s (Healy Onstage 48/32 WAV) + FR-AV2 > Neumann KM-184s (ORTF FOB 48/32 WAV) [1]. Also: Brandon Eggleston and the band supported the livetaping of this performance [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by Taft Theatre: [The Mountain Goats – Friday, August 14, 2026](https://tafttheatre.org/events/2026/08/the-mountain-goats) [3]\n- Poster by Cincy Groove: [The Mountain Goats Announce New Album & Share Lead Single \"Charlie Sheen Reaches Out To The Feds\" - Coming To The Taft T](https://cincygroove.com/2026/05/19/the-mountain-goats-announce-new-album-share-lead-single-charlie-sheen-reaches-out-to-the-feds-coming-to-the-taft-theatre-on-8-14/) [4]",
